From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:29:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(telemetry): attribute spans to the acting user and
 runner

On a multi-user server, exported spans only carried session.id, so
answering "whose traffic is this?" or "which runner is slow?" needed a
join against the Omnigent database. The user and runner were already
bound in the debug-logging context for every request; stamp them on
spans too.

- omnigent.runner.id: the runner bound to the request, falling back to
  OMNIGENT_RUNNER_ID in runner and harness processes.
- enduser.id (OTel semconv): the authenticated user on the server, and
  the process owner on host/runner/harness. Opt-in via
  OMNIGENT_OTEL_CAPTURE_USER because the id is usually an email. The
  server middleware also stamps the root HTTP span, which starts before
  auth resolves the user.

Refs #10794

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
